	"title": "a program fits a runner when the runner takes its type or a type it conforms to, by the nearest ermine/types. its type: by its path (a string, a list), its ermine.type, else the extension of its name (main.c: public.c-source; notes.txt: public.plain-text); by id, its ermine.type; carried, the type given. a runner taking public.source-code runs public.c-source (from the extension, from ermine.type, by id, carried) and loads it; not a supertype (plain text), a type the folder does not have, a node whose ermine.type says otherwise than its name (fake.c, plain text), a node by id with no ermine.type: wrong-form, the type when there is one. in a box over apps, which sees no ermine/types: no extension's type, and conformance is only the type itself",
